Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(cortensor): honor tool_call_strategy fallback parsing and reuse http_client

Fixes two bugs in CortensorProvider (openminion==0.1.24):
1. _parse_response_payload() hardcoded fallback_enabled=False while ignoring
   tool_call_strategy, silently dropping all fallback JSON tool calls returned
   by /api/v2/completions even though _build_completion_prompt() injects the
   tool-calling JSON contract.
2. _complete_via_openai_chat_mode() omitted http_client=http_client_for_config(...),
   silently disabling HTTP connection reuse compared to _complete_via_completion_mode().
diff --git a/src/openminion/modules/llm/providers/cortensor/adapter.py b/src/openminion/modules/llm/providers/cortensor/adapter.py
--- a/src/openminion/modules/llm/providers/cortensor/adapter.py
+++ b/src/openminion/modules/llm/providers/cortensor/adapter.py
@@ -275,6 +275,7 @@
             ),
             trace_metadata=request.metadata,
             env=config.get("__env__"),
+            http_client=http_client_for_config(self._http_client, config),
             telemetryctl=config.get("telemetryctl"),
         )
 
@@ -467,7 +468,9 @@
             provider_name=self.name,
             model_name=str(response_payload.get("model") or fallback_model),
             allowed_tool_names=allowed_tool_names if request.tools else None,
-            fallback_enabled=False,
+            fallback_enabled=bool(
+                request.tools and supports_fallback_tool_calling(tool_call_strategy)
+            ),
             parser_plugin_selection=behavior_profile.parser_plugin_selection,
             fallback_parser_policy=behavior_profile.fallback_parser_policy,
         )
